Fixed asset utilization and management;

Other responsibilities assigned by the supervisor.

Requirements

* 3-5 years relevant working experiences with Can-do Attitude 

* Excellent English and Chinese communication skills 

* Experienced with Policy design and optimizing

* Well-organized, responsible, detail-minded, hardworking as a quick learner

* Be able to handle multi-tasks under pressure 

* Experience in procurement / HR is a plus

**Responsibilities:**

Together with the Marketing Strategy Lead execute regional growth campaigns in partnership with local & central stakeholders to ensure business objectives (KPIs) are met;

Drive and lead growth marketing promotions across the CIS/CEE (incl. Balkans) targeting users' stickiness, and platform ecosystem usage (Lifecycle, Product Marketing, Active Users Growth Hacks via Retention, Reactivation, Stickiness);

Establish marketing best practices (including segmentation, and A/B testing strategies) using data-driven insights; Measure, understand, and report critical metrics progress to regional management & Central Leaders;

Develop marketing strategies aimed at maximizing the long-term value of clients through customer segmentation, personalization, automated user journeys, and the ideal combination of products and distribution channels;

Map out the user journey and increase user funnel conversion through surfacing product asks, user education, and operational campaign (top focus on KYC-Deposit-Trades conversion);

Monitor campaign progress and results using data analysis and user feedback to ensure ever-improving efficiency and user experience;

Act as a driver for platform innovations (products, UX/UI), community needs solutions (Optimizations, Bonus Systems), in-depth analytics & in-sight sharing.

**Requirements:**

3-5+ years of experience in Growth/Digital/Marketing departments;

Data-oriented mindset connecting actionable insights (data) and exact drivers (campaigns). Strong analytical capabilities related to user behavior analysis, and user retention strategy development in marketing funnels;

Execution-oriented professional - with the humility, drive, and scrappiness to get it done;

Experience in launching both large-scale and targeted campaigns throughout the user conversion funnel OR product optimization;

Well-versed and ideally skilled in all 3 areas: Marketing Growth Hacking/Operational Management/Data Analytics;

Preferably experience in user segmentation, customer lifecycle management, and A/B testing;

Must have a strong interest in crypto/blockchain/technology, Crypto enthusiast is a plus;

Must be able to work independently and execute initiatives from A to Z;

Proven experience in growing and managing user base supported by strong coordination skills and strategic mindset for marketing;

Creative thinking for developing innovative product organizational strategies and engaging campaigns.

We are looking for a Marketing Manager for Kyrgyzstan who will take full ownership of local marketing campaigns. This role is for those who would like to drive crypto education through Kyrgyz market.

Responsibilities:

- Take full ownership of KG regional marketing, from business strategy to marketing on-hands daily execution;
- Develop and execute non-standard marketing initiatives that resonate with local culture and users;
- Sign sponsorship projects and execute them independently;
- Design and execute user growth campaigns across acquisition, activation, and retention;
- Build and strengthen community engagement, working closely with Binance Angels and local partners;
- Organize and manage offline and online events (meetups, roadshows, collaborations);
- Manage local marketing budgets, ensuring efficient allocation and ROI;
- Deliver timely and clear reporting and accountability on campaign performance;
- Collaborate cross-functionally with global and product marketing teams to localize campaigns.

Requirements:

- Minimum 2 years of relevant marketing experience (Web3, fintech, or agency background preferred);
- Proven track record in campaign management, community building, or brand management;
- Bilingual English/Kyrgyz is required to be able to coordinate with overseas partners and stakeholders. Russian is nice to have;
- Strong analytical skills, with the ability to translate insights into actions; 
- Comfortable taking full ownership and operating with accountability; 
- Based in Kyrgyzstan with a wide network within the country is a must;
- Previous experience working in a Web3/crypto marketing agency or startup is highly desirable.

Nice to have and more about the role:

- Experience working in fast-scaling tech or fintech companies; 
- Hands-on experience with local PR, influencers, or grassroots communities;
- A mid-level role with full ownership of marketing in Kazakhstan, this role requires execution skills;
- No direct reports are allocated; 
- The opportunity to shape the regional strategy and community presence from the ground up; 
- A highly dynamic, international environment with the world’s leading crypto brand; 
- Cross-regional collaboration with global marketing and product teams.

Product Manager IC-02

What you’ll do

Responsibilities

Define product strategy and lead cross-functional initiatives across reporting, data infrastructure and artificial intelligence to support internal teams at Stripe;

Drive the development of internal GenAI applications, including use case scoping, vendor evaluation, data readiness, and change management for operational adoption;

Conduct technical and business feasibility analysis for data center localization to support Stripe’s global expansion, addressing compliance, latency, and operational readiness; Lead efforts to platformize reporting by building reusable data models and internal tools that scale across multiple product and finance use cases;

Oversee the development of a semantic layer to standardize key metrics and accelerate self-service analytics for data consumers;

Collaborate closely with engineering, data science, legal, and compliance teams to ensure scalable, secure, and efficient product delivery.

Who you are

Minimum requirements

Bachelor’s degree or foreign equivalent in engineering or a related field, followed by 3 years of experience in product design or engineering.

Position also requires the following: 

3 years of experience driving end-to-end product requirements across multiple teams;

3 years of experience in gathering and prioritizing complex deliverables while engaging with customers, managing technical and business trade-offs, and collaborating in a cross-functional environment with customers, business leaders, and technical teams to deliver complex data and platform products in the fintech industry;

3 years of experience working on user interface (UI) and user experience (UX) principles and best practices;

3 years of experience with software product management;

3 years of experience Utilizing data to manage metric, drive process improvement, and implement business cases;

3 years of experience in developing company-wide product roadmaps, generating feature requirements, and executing go-to-market strategies; and

2 years of experience building Gen AI applications for fintech industry.

Data Scientist

What you’ll do

Responsibilities

Apply statistical, time series forecasting and machine learning models on large datasets to predict future performance of users or products.

Partner closely with Sales and Data Science teams to identify important questions and answer them with data.

Design, implement and launch data science solutions using Python and R to empower data-driven decisions and products at scale.

Create analyses that generate insights for business teams.

Design, analyze, and interpret the results of experiments.

Build ETL data transformation pipelines in SQL.

Who you are

Minimum requirements

Must have a Master's degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Business Analytics, Statistics, or a related quantitative field, plus 3 years of experience in a Data Scientist or related occupation.

3 years of experience building ETL data transformation pipelines in SQL;

3 years of experience working closely with product and business teams to identify important questions and answer them with data;

2 years of experience productionalizing and implementing machine learning models;

2 years of experience productionalizing and implementing software products;

2 years of experience designing, analyzing, and interpreting the results of experiments;

2 years of experience designing, and analyzing software architectures;

2 years of experience designing, implementing, and launching data science solutions;

2 years of experience designing, implementing, and launching software solutions; and

2 years of experience applying statistical and machine learning models on large datasets to predict future performance of users or products.

